    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12154" root="دجن" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُجْنَةٌ</span></b>  [or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُجُنَّةٌ</span></b>  ?] <i>Rain:</i> so in the phrase
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَوْمٌ ذُو دُجْنَةٍ</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُجُنَّةٍ</span> ?] <i>a day of rain;</i> as also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذُو دُغْنَةٍ</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُغُنَّةٍ</span>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُجُنَّةٍ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
Also, (S, K,) in the colours of camels, (S,) The
<i>ugliest kind of blackness.</i> (S, K.)

